## Build System

{# lede #}This document covers the **Build System** APIs{# lede #}.

Basically, the build system is governed by two user-supplied Perl modules: [`lib/path.pm`](https://github.com/SunStarSys/www.iconoclasts.blog/blob/trunk/lib/path.pm) and [`lib/view.pm`](https://github.com/SunStarSys/www.iconoclasts.blog/blob/trunk/lib/view.pm).

The former's job is to do three things:

0. load [`lib/facts.yml`](https://github.com/SunStarSys/www.iconoclasts.blog/blob/trunk/lib/facts.yml) and [`lib/acl.yml`](https://github.com/SunStarSys/www.iconoclasts.blog/blob/trunk/lib/acl.yml),
1. construct `@path::patterns`, and
2. opportunistically walk the `content/` tree to seed `%path::dependencies` and `@path::acls` from markdown/yaml file header metadata.

The latter's job is to provide invokable `view`-based `$method`s for the matching entries in `@path::patterns` (as a stringified method name in the second slot of each arrayref entry), invoked by the [build scripting]({{snippetA.pretty_uri}}):

[snippet:repo=SunStarSys/orion:path=build_site.pl:token=#api:lang=perl]

Many views are meant to be stacked as "filters" to preprocess aspects of the file in `$path` that are novel, like external code `snippets` or `asymptote`-fenced markdown blocks. You can see an example of that [here](https://github.com/SunStarSys/www.iconoclasts.blog/blob/trunk/lib/path.pm#L53).

[TOC]

